.TH S3AR-DELETE 1 "September 2026" "s3ar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3ar-delete \- delete S3 objects and buckets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3ar-delete
.RB [ \-v | \-vv | \-vvv ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry-run ]
.I s3://[BUCKET[/KEY]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s3ar-delete
lists and deletes matching resources in one pass, without prompting for
confirmation.
It permanently removes object versions and delete markers, aborts matching
multipart uploads, and removes selected buckets after they are empty.
.PP
.B s3://
selects every bucket visible to the configured credentials.
.B s3://BUCKET
and
.B s3://BUCKET/
select one entire bucket.
.B s3://BUCKET/KEY
selects only the exact object key.
.B s3://BUCKET/PREFIX/
selects keys beginning with PREFIX/ and keeps the bucket.
For example, 
.B s3://photos/photo
does not select photo1 or photo/a, while
.B s3://photos/photo/
selects photo/a but not photo or photo1.
.PP
Deletion stops on the first S3 error. Objects protected by retention or legal
hold cannot be deleted until their protection is removed. Objects added while
the command runs may remain, so the operation is not an atomic snapshot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show each matching resource. Repeat twice for debug messages or three times
for S3 request tracing. A summary is printed without verbosity. Send
.B SIGUSR1
to increase verbosity while running, or
.B SIGUSR2
to decrease it.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
List resources that would be deleted without changing S3.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully, or dry run completed.
.TP
.B 2
A fatal error occurred, including invalid arguments, a configuration error,
or an S3 failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3ar (1),
.BR s3ar-get (1),
.BR s3ar-put (1)
